:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=CHKCMNTRC.Check Communications Trace (CHKCMNTRC)
:P.The Check Communications Trace (CHKCMNTRC) command works with the
status of the traces.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKCMNTRC/CFGOBJ'.Configuration object (CFGOBJ)
:P.The configuration object&colon. a line, controller or device
description, or a network server or interface description.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKCMNTRC/CFGTYPE'.Type (CFGTYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIN, *NWI, *NWS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTCMNTRC.Delete Communications Trace (DLTCMNTRC)
:P.Use the Delete Communications Trace (DLTCMNTRC) command to delete an
ended trace and its data.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTCMNTRC/CFGOBJ'.Configuration object (CFGOBJ)
:P.The configuration object&colon. a line, controller or device
description, or a network server or interface description.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTCMNTRC/CFGTYPE'.Type (CFGTYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIN, *NWI, *NWS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDCMNTRC.End Communications Trace (ENDCMNTRC)
:P.Use the End Communications Trace (ENDCMNTRC) command to stop a trace,
keeping its data.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDCMNTRC/CFGOBJ'.Configuration object (CFGOBJ)
:P.The configuration object&colon. a line, controller or device
description, or a network server or interface description.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDCMNTRC/CFGTYPE'.Type (CFGTYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIN, *NWI, *NWS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PRTCMNTRC.Print Communications Trace (PRTCMNTRC)
:P.The Print Communications Trace (PRTCMNTRC) command works with a
trace's frames, decoded, to a spooled file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTCMNTRC/CFGOBJ'.Configuration object (CFGOBJ)
:P.The configuration object&colon. a line, controller or device
description, or a network server or interface description.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTCMNTRC/CFGTYPE'.Type (CFGTYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIN, *NWI, *NWS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTCMNTRC/CTLD'.Controller (CTLD)
:P.The controller for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTCMNTRC/CODE'.Character code (CODE)
:P.The character code for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EBCDIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTCMNTRC/FMTTCP'.Format TCP/IP data (FMTTCP)
:P.Whether to format TCP/IP data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTCMNTRC/TCPIPADR'.IP address (TCPIPADR)
:P.The IP address for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. IP address
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. IP address
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTCMNTRC/SLTPORT'.IP port number (SLTPORT)
:P.The IP port number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTCMNTRC/FMTBCST'.Format broadcast data (FMTBCST)
:P.Whether to format broadcast data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRCMNTRC.Start Communications Trace (STRCMNTRC)
:P.Use the Start Communications Trace (STRCMNTRC) command to start
tracing a line's frames.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMNTRC/CFGOBJ'.Configuration object (CFGOBJ)
:P.The configuration object&colon. a line, controller or device
description, or a network server or interface description.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMNTRC/CFGTYPE'.Type (CFGTYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIN, *NWI, *NWS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMNTRC/MAXSTG'.Buffer size (MAXSTG)
:P.The most auxiliary storage, in kilobytes, the user's objects may
occupy.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MAX:EPK.
:PD.The largest value.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be 128K, 256K, 512K, 1M, 2M, 4M, 8M, 16M, 32M, 64M,
128M, 256M, 512M, 1G.
:P.When no value is given, 128K is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMNTRC/DTADIR'.Data direction (DTADIR)
:P.The data direction for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BOTH:EPK.
:PD.Both.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SND, *RCV.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMNTRC/TRCFULL'.Trace full (TRCFULL)
:P.The trace full for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:PT.:PK.*STOPTRC:EPK.
:PD.When full, the trace stops.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMNTRC/USRDTA'.Number of user bytes to trace (USRDTA)
:P.User data, up to 10 characters, kept with the object.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*MAX:EPK.
:PD.The largest value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRCMNTRC/TEXT'.Trace description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
